Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||07-23-2001||10:40 AM||||I have a strut-tower brace on my '87 GT, it did make a little difference in the cornering stability, but not drastic.  You can attach the bar straight on, or "pre-load" it for better performance. I spoke to someone who said that if you have Koni Adjustables, it makes a little more difference.  I'll try to post some photos of it when my digital camera batteries are fully re-charged.<P>As for where to get them from... here in Minnesota, one of our club member is a engineer/machinist and makes them for '84-'87 and for '88s.  I'm not sure exactly what he charges- probably about $125-$150. I got mine in a part trade. Anyway- contact Darrel Morse @ (763)441-5679 He's in Elk River Minnesota- and he's "the man"  (he has other performance machined products as well...)!<P>Thanks-<BR>Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||07-23-2001||11:23 AM||||Ok, here are the photos of my strut tower brace... a little wet this morning, but I drive it everyday rain or shine!  (these photos are posted from my photopoint stuff, so I'm not entirely sure it's going to work.  If not, email me and I'll email the photos directly to you!  (if you email me at rob@xtralite.com I'll get it right away!)<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/minnfieros/strut1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Strut photo 1</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/minnfieros/strut2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Strut photo 2</A> <P>Check this out... might be funny to you too.  This guy parked his real (I checked) Ferrari F355 Spyder outside this morning with the top down- and it's been raining on & off all morning!  That's definitely the way to treat a $195K vehicle... what's a little water on Italian leather! Still a pretty nice car!<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/minnfieros/f355wet.jpg" TARGET=_blank>ferrari photo</A> <P>Thanks-<BR>Rob Bartlett<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/minnfieros/grngt.jpg" TARGET=_blank>My Car Too!</A><BR>______________________________<BR>OK, I'm hating this whole photopoint issue, I'm going to have to upload the photos somewhere else for this to work!  Just email me if you want to see them!<BR>_________________________________<BR>OK, I've reloaded the photos to geocities, hopefully this will work now!<BR>__________________________________<BR>Aarrgh!  OK, frustration has set in. I'm not sure why none of this works, but if you click the link for the photos, then copy and re-paste the link-deleting the "http://", the picts should appear.  I still am not understanding this...guess I'm misunderstanding something!<P><BR>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 07-23-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||1
